{
  /* THE PRODUCTION IMAGE BUILD, and the one thing it may not typecheck.
   *
   * `docker/nginx/Dockerfile` builds `dist/` from a context that deliberately
   * EXCLUDES `server/` — `.dockerignore` measures the saving at ~584 MB of
   * node_modules per build. But `tsconfig.app.json` includes all of `src`,
   * test files and all, and the conformance tests in `src/lib/automerge/`
   * import the SERVER's copy of a shared module on purpose so that a divergence
   * fails `tsc` instead of drifting silently (a comment claiming a gate exists
   * is worse than no comment).
   *
   * COUNTS DROPPED 2026-09-04, not recounted. This said "277 test files, and
   * two of those import"; on the merge day it was 285 and THREE
   * (`workspaceBinding.conformance.test.ts` was the third, and the sentence had
   * not moved). A number nobody recomputes goes stale silently, and neither
   * number was load-bearing: `src/webImageBuild.test.ts` derives both sets by
   * walking `src`, so the set is measured on every run rather than transcribed
   * here.
   *
   * Those two facts are individually right and jointly fatal: the image build
   * failed `TS2307: Cannot find module '../../../server/src/...'` from the day
   * the conformance suite landed (2026-08-20) until the next deploy tried
   * (2026-08-24) — four days in which every gate the repository runs was green,
   * because CI runs `npm run build` at the repository root, where `server/`
   * exists.
   *
   * The resolution is NOT to weaken the gate and NOT to drag the server's
   * dependency graph into the web image. A test file is never shipped in
   * `dist/`, so typechecking it is not this build's job; it is `npm run
   * build`'s, which still does it in CI and locally against the whole tree.
   * This config is that split, and nothing else — `src/webImageBuild.test.ts`
   * asserts it differs from `tsconfig.app.json` by the exclusion alone, so a
   * compiler option added there cannot quietly stop applying to the artifact
   * that actually reaches users.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    /* Its own, so a local run cannot hand this config the app config's
     * incremental state or the other way round. */
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.image.tsbuildinfo"
  },
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/**/*.test.tsx"]
}
